    "system": {
        "type": "basic",
        "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Price</strong> 25 bx; <strong>Weight</strong> 0.2 lb.;</p><p>Often manufactured using gurwraith or the bark of climbing vines like birchbane, poison comes in single-dose glass vials. As <span class=\"cosmere-icon\">1</span>, you can pour it into food, liquid, or a container, or you can apply the poison to a melee weapon or a piece of ammunition you’re holding. When you do, the GM may require you to succeed on a [[test skill=stl]] to avoid discovery. When a character ingests the poison or is hit by an attack using the poisoned weapon or ammunition, the poison is expended, and the character suffers the following effects:</p><p><strong>Effectual Poison.</strong> The target must succeed on a [[test dc=14 skill=ath]] test or take [[damage 2d8 Vital]] and be @UUID[Compendium.cosmere-rpg-mistborn-handbook.handbook.JournalEntry.b684FTgeTTE90HLs.JournalEntryPage.vyYzxzfhwORSeTLw#stunned]{Stunned} for 1 hour.</p>",
            "chat": "",
            "short": ""
        },
